    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43744" root="&#xA;                        منى&#xA;                    " body-key="m1">
                        
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُنْيَةٌ</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>A thing wished for</i> by a man: pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُنًى</span>.
(T.) This word and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُمْنِيَّةٌ</span></b>  signify the same.
(M, Mgh, Msb, K.) See an ex. in a verse cited
voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَوْ</span> ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المُنْيَةُ</span> in the case of a covered she-camel, <i>The period by the end of which one knows
whether she be pregnant or not.</i> (M.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُنْيَةٌ</span> of
a mare, <i>Twenty days.</i> (M, voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَفُودٌ</span>.)

